From e6471463dfc03fb7abe56dada858ba449bc4129e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 15:34:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 108/109] dynarmic: the persistent code cache for both JITs
 (A32 and A64)

The A32 JIT's code cache moves to backend/x64/jit_code_cache.h, a template over the emitter and the
guest address width that both JITs use; each keeps what is its own (the build and configuration
fingerprints, the objects its code may point into). The A64 JIT gets SaveCodeCache, LoadCodeCache
and GetCodeCacheUse as the A32 one, with UserConfig::code_cache_objects; its objects include the
system registers it is given (TPIDR_EL0, TPIDRRO_EL0) and its page table at its address space's
size. The file format is version 2 (guest ranges 64 bits wide). Per-core translation counts for
the A64 JIT too. (The desktop harness's fixed code cache address applies to code caches only.)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01REmpC53sSK3VTcKMxWFSSb
